lines=['# Assessment B: independent mechanical composition baseline','', 'The latest user explicitly rejects prior block-placement acceptance. This document diagnoses the historical 36-game baseline independently from assessment A; it is not an approval of current work. No product file was edited, no browser was started, and no assessment A findings were read or exchanged.','', '## Evidence and limits','', '- Individually inspected all 72 actual originals: 36 TV 1920×1080 and 36 native-controller browser phone 402×874. The phone PNGs are 1206×2622 at DPR3; the viewer resized them to942×2048 for delivery. Full original files and hashes are retained in the JSON manifest.','- Baseline: `output/playwright/ui-rework-2026-10-02/final-catalog-1734/report.json`; gallery17807 is only a navigation surface. Direct original files were the review evidence.','- Historical report has real engine/bot normal-clock states, errors[] and changedFiles[]. Those facts prove execution/coherence of that capture, not good composition.','- Metadata was sampled before screenshots. Push/Shrink originals already show Out while metadata still has a joystick; Flappy also shows Out. Geometry must not be presented as synchronized PNG bounds. Historical capture UI phase is not the exact local controller state.','- No physical iPhone interaction, safe-area, keyboard or touch verification is claimed. Browser originals establish visible layout, not hardware ergonomics.','- Current source has '+str(len(packet['allBaselineSourceDrift']))+' changed paths among332 recorded baseline paths at manifest generation. Per-engine and shared SHA comparisons are in `mechanical-evidence/all36-baseline.json`. Baseline findings remain historical targets; current acceptance requires fresh source-bound captures.','', '## Actual source/tool assessment','', 'Read AGENTS.md, design-contract-2026.md, ui-regression-rules.md, Impeccable SKILL/layout reference; applied mobile-native hardware/evidence separation and Emil grouping/priority principles. Ran Impeccable context exactly once in this fresh task against public/tv.html; it succeeded. PRODUCT.md\'s prior bottom-rankings-only scope is stale and superseded by the user\'s latest ALL36 request; no context repair was performed.','', 'Expanded bounded detector scan to21 named HTML files: the launcher plus20 unique engine host documents covering all36 catalog routes. Exit2 means findings, not unavailable. Exact15 warnings:4 nested-card heuristics and11 cramped-padding heuristics; line0/static markup cannot establish rendered severity. Saved raw output in `mechanical-evidence/detector-layout.json`. The initial14-file run had the same15 warnings; the earlier verbal count16 was corrected to root.','', 'Host route lookup confirms /host→public/index.html for quiz/naval/crocodile/drawguess/tabletop; Monster root uses public/index.html; Bow /tv→public/tv.html. Party/arcade variants share engine hosts, rather than pretending36 different markup files exist.','', '### Source relationships that require coordination','', '| Before | After (proposal, no source edits) | Why |','| --- | --- | --- |','| public/tv.js uses hardcoded fieldGutter12 for22 IDs, creating18 physical px at1080p | A semantic field/backdrop reservation negotiated with each game | A receiver wall strip does not belong to the game world and is visibly discontinuous in many canvas scenes |','| Shared centered notch156px overlays an iframe that starts at0/18px; right stats often occupy live world | Measured title/stats exclusion that respects the actual field and non-playable rail | Canvas rectangle overlap is only a candidate; Flappy original proves a pipe is actually covered |','| Screen-centered title coexists with left-biased game field in Kart/Jenga/Crane/Duel | One explicit field axis or a purposeful rail header shared by title/status | Different axes create a detached heading unless the rail is intentionally the title owner |','| Question/answers and roster top anchored in Quiz/Millionaire | Center complete reading/answer group in remaining stage | A blank lower450px is not useful gameplay space for a quiz; question/answers should lead the available area |','| Some phone layouts center a control or repeat status cards independently | Center the complete current-task/status/control group in the actual iframe | The usable child viewport is664px, not874px; fixed header/footer already reserve their area |','| Bottom full-width player cards repeat individual player/world names | Compact roster dock or field-related identities with one clearly owned score region | A second strong horizontal strip competes with field, even if every pixel technically fits |','', '## Per-game independent findings','', 'Each row is a reasoned rendered finding or a qualified preserve direction. P1 marks a visible major task/hierarchy problem or HUD covering authoritative playing geometry; P2 marks a bounded grouping/axis/rhythm issue. No row is a blanket PASS.','', '| Game | Priority | TV original: before | Phone original: before | Proposed relationship / after |','| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |']
